#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157021 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "35acfa60-3395-5f11-94f9-627499386932" :question/math-academy-id "e-7159" :question/problem "Given the sets $X = \\{ 2, 5, 7, 8 \\},$ $Y = \\{ 1, 3, 5 \\},$ and $Z = \\{ 2, 4, 6, 8 \\},$ find $X \\setminus Y,$ $Y \\setminus Z,$ and $Z \\setminus X.$" :question/worked-solution "The set $X \\setminus Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the element $5 \\in Y$ is also in $X,$ so we must remove it. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∖Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={2,5,7,8}-{1,3,5} \\\\  & ={2,7,8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Y \\setminus Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $Z.$ Note that none of the elements of $Y$ are in $Z.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∖Z & =Y-Z \\\\  & ={1,3,5}-{2,4,6,8} \\\\  & ={1,3,5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe set $Z \\setminus X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Z$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $2,8 \\in Z$ are also in $X,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z∖X & =Z-X \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8}-{2,5,7,8} \\\\  & ={4,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157022 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/id #uuid "89c94a89-21de-5a4f-a365-85701b2e4ef2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7160" :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0.$ What is $A \\setminus B?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{ 6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\setminus B$ is the *difference* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $A$ but *not* in $B.$\n\nThe elements of $A$ that are also in $B$ are $12, 24, 36$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $A.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∖B & =A-B \\\\  & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…}-{6,12,18,24,30,36,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,28,32,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "9e0d2770-a884-558f-becb-a38fe709b2a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-7167" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/96cd980d105fe04d2169f9252aa2e7e08bf57ba18cf7d7808d0c4c98c83f7767.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X.$ To represent $Y \\setminus X,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/5461edca3823f1cafd9f7b51528cd6eb1035e38f7f94c60177e369e2cdd5f350.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{ 4 \\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4687dcd7-a5ab-5dc6-be6d-89d806a61a02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf1b1061-5741-59d8-a418-ceda12486338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,♢}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296424} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbbe227-245b-50c1-b20d-ddb6bfe70b54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,◻,♣,♡}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296425} {:answer/id #uuid "942a9098-88e6-5763-89c4-6b4c5ddf6534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♣}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296426} {:answer/id #uuid "fd5d56bc-47e6-5789-bd05-4f2c1efb6494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{△,◻,♠}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296427} {:answer/id #uuid "4abc2d44-192f-57ff-b76b-98726c327864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,♢,♣}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf1b1061-5741-59d8-a418-ceda12486338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{♠,♢}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296424} :answer-field/id #uuid "551fbd58-5433-5802-8da1-414f635af75f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "faa23ac8-04a3-5479-a9d4-ad113271640a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105200" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/a50acd7e54d52f6284962cb81a5f662321b045a5d533470186719ad2a91ab18b.png)\n\nGiven the sets $Y={△,◻,♣,♡}$ and  $Z={△,◻,♡,♢,♠}$ shown above, find $Z∖Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $Z∖Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $Z$ but not $Y.$ To represent $Z∖Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Z$ but not $Y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/45a15beb8833e2974706a04b0cdfd81dcdda4b92323f0c092683b9882e53b0ea.png)\n\nThe elements $♠$ and $♢$ are in $Z$  but not $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nZ∖Y={♠,♢}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a9bf1c3-c25e-546d-bf50-f506b6cb2bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,16,20,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296501} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5b5b4e-290f-541c-ba2f-6ba2982c59cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{12,24…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296502} {:answer/id #uuid "d4685bed-f4c4-5ce4-b803-08ec3f7b9daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,6,9,15,18,21,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296503} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3343f8-3a82-58af-bc78-065391a8604e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3,4,6,8,9,15,16,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296504} {:answer/id #uuid "0db51cb2-8bf8-5b33-a63b-bc763b47289f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,3,6,9,15,18,21,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a9bf1c3-c25e-546d-bf50-f506b6cb2bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,8,16,20,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296501} :answer-field/id #uuid "af625279-b9b8-5e8b-9297-c5d5fbef4f97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4c54f56-ff83-5c5e-b062-1e1004f84f48" :question/math-academy-id "q-81766" :question/problem "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $B-A?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}-{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
